# The first real admin accounts. Fill this in, create the accounts once, then delete the file.
#
#   1. Copy it:   cp deploy/first-admins.env.example first-admins.env   (in the repo root; it is git-ignored)
#   2. Fill in at least slot 1.
#   3. Run:
#        on your computer:  npm run db:create-admins
#        on the server:     docker compose run --rm create-admins
#   4. Delete first-admins.env. The passwords are stored hashed in the database; the file is no longer needed.
#
# Rules
#   - ROLE is one of: Super Administrator, Event Manager, Registration Manager, Finance Manager, Content Manager, Viewer.
#     Leave it empty for Super Administrator.
#   - PASSWORD needs at least 12 characters. Use a long one; two-step login is added before launch.
#   - Do not put quotes around values. A password may contain spaces and symbols but not a # sign.
#   - Accounts that already exist are skipped, so running it twice does no harm. It never changes an existing password.
#   - Leave slots you do not need empty (up to 10 slots, ADMIN_1 to ADMIN_10).
#   - Never use @gyn.test addresses. Those are the demo accounts for development only.

ADMIN_1_EMAIL=
ADMIN_1_NAME=
ADMIN_1_ROLE=Super Administrator
ADMIN_1_PASSWORD=

ADMIN_2_EMAIL=
ADMIN_2_NAME=
ADMIN_2_ROLE=
ADMIN_2_PASSWORD=

ADMIN_3_EMAIL=
ADMIN_3_NAME=
ADMIN_3_ROLE=
ADMIN_3_PASSWORD=
